messages:
lisa: opened a PR to tidy up function-calling examples and structured-output guidance. link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/501

mike: skimmed. looks promising. couple asks: include migration notes for customers on the old tool-caller API and add a tiny test harness that asserts our canonical examples parse.

lisa: yep planning both. sara can you do node snippets + a lightweight parse helper? i already added python examples.

sara: taking node. adding parseWithFallback snippet and a tiny mocha test that runs in CI. also fixed a broken internal link that pointed to /docs/old-tool. updated to /docs/function-calling/migration.

kevin: on the JSON schema in the docs: avoid marking deep fields as required. recommend using oneOf for payload variants and document validator behavior. sample snippet I propose:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "type": {"type": "string"},
    "data": {
      "oneOf": [ {"$ref": "#/definitions/create"}, {"$ref": "#/definitions/lookup"} ]
    }
  },
  "required": ["type"]
}
```

ben: also add an explicit example of a malformed model response and how to recover. customers repeatedly hit silent failures when the model returns unexpected keys. suggested node fallback:

```js
function parseWithFallback(text) {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(text);
  } catch(e) {
    // fallback: quick kv parse + telemetry
    const m = /action:\s*(\w+)/i.exec(text);
    return m ? {action: m[1], fallback: true} : null;
  }
}
```

sara: adding that to node SDK example and the migration guide. also including a short diff so integrators can update fast:

```diff
- tools: [{name: 'search', input_schema: {q: 'string'}}]
+ functions: [{name: 'search', input_schema: {query: 'string'}}]
```

lisa: nice. can we also add guidance text that we shouldn't claim perfect enforcement? suggest: 'Use schema validation and runtime checks to detect drift; prefer safe fallbacks and clear telemetry.'

kevin: agreed. reworded the guardrails paragraph in the PR to be less absolute. added note about token limits and KV cache interactions.

mike: docs-ops: can we run a link sweep before merge? I found a couple more internal links while editing. @doc-bot any chance of preview + link-check?

doc-bot: preview deployed: https://preview.docs.redwood.ai/pr-501  link-check queued (job 7901).

lisa: plan: kevin will fix one flaky example test, mike will do final review, then merge and run final sweep. i'll post a short Slack release note and update SDK changelogs after merge.

kevin: looking into the flaky test now  likely whitespace/formatting in an example. small patch incoming.

mike: if tests pass i'm happy to merge tomorrow morning. low-risk change with good clarity for customers. :shipit:

lisa: thanks all. after merge i'll add the short migration FAQ to the docs landing page and ping support so they can help customers update.

ben: one last request: include a tiny example of telemetry events we recommend for parse failures (event name, minimal properties) so customers can mirror it.

sara: added a suggested telemetry JSON and a tiny sample log line to the doc.

doc-bot: merge-ready check: all checks passing except flaky example test (CI #1302). flagged for manual review.

kevin: patched the test. re-running CI.

lisa: excellent. aiming to merge once CI is green and link-check passes.

mike: sounds good. thanks everyone! :tada:
